pan style=\"color:#000\"><br>p </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#Note that the colors are inverted. t1 to t5 should be blue, not red, and the contrary for t6 to t10. Is this a bug?</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>And color OTUS</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\">#Colored OTUS</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>cls </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;t1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;t2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;t8&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;t7&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            c2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;t3&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;t4&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;t10&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            c3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;t9&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;t6&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;t5&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>tree1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> groupOTU</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cls</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggtree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tree1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        scale_color_manual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">values</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;black&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;green&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;blue&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>But I&#39;m unable to combine them?</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\">#Combined?</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&lt;+%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_tippoint</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">place</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p2<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Error</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Insufficient</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> values </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> manual scale</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> needed but only </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> provided</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>How can I create plots in which the edges have certain color and the tip a different one? Why is the order of the colors in p inverted?</div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
